    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; margin: 16pt 0;" /><h2 style="color: #0369a1; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold; border-bottom: 1pt solid #bae6fd; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid;">18. 📅 DEVELOPMENT TIMELINE & MILESTONES</h2><table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 12pt 0; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;"><tr style="background-color: #0284c7; color: #ffffff; font-weight: bold; text-align: left;"><th style="padding: 8pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #0284c7; font-size: 10.5pt;">Phase</th><th style="padding: 8pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #0284c7; font-size: 10.5pt;">Milestone Objective</th><th style="padding: 8pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #0284c7; font-size: 10.5pt;">Key Deliverables & Main Work</th><th style="padding: 8pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #0284c7; font-size: 10.5pt;">Output Artifact</th></tr><tr style="background-color: #ffffff; border-bottom: 1pt solid #e2e8f0;"><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><strong>Phase 1</strong></td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Requirement Analysis</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Domain research & feature list definition</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Feature Specification Sheet</td></tr><tr style="background-color: #f8fafc; border-bottom: 1pt solid #e2e8f0;"><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><strong>Phase 2</strong></td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">System Architecture</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Folder structure layout & JSON database schema design</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">data/portfolio.json</code> baseline</td></tr><tr style="background-color: #ffffff; border-bottom: 1pt solid #e2e8f0;"><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><strong>Phase 3</strong></td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Frontend UI Development</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Glassmorphic HTML/CSS design & layout creation</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">index.php</code> & <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">styles.css</code></td></tr><tr style="background-color: #f8fafc; border-bottom: 1pt solid #e2e8f0;"><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><strong>Phase 4</strong></td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Interactive Features</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Modals, search bars, year/category filter scripts</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">script.js</code></td></tr><tr style="background-color: #ffffff; border-bottom: 1pt solid #e2e8f0;"><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><strong>Phase 5</strong></td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Backend API & Auth</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">REST controller endpoints & BCRYPT login system</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/api.php</code> & <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/login.php</code></td></tr><tr style="background-color: #f8fafc; border-bottom: 1pt solid #e2e8f0;"><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><strong>Phase 6</strong></td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Admin Dashboard</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">10-tab desktop CMS layout & modal form builder</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/index.php</code></td></tr><tr style="background-color: #ffffff; border-bottom: 1pt solid #e2e8f0;"><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><strong>Phase 7</strong></td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Refinement & Bug Fixing</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Zero-scroll fixed table ratios & exact category filtering</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Codebase updates</td></tr><tr style="background-color: #f8fafc; border-bottom: 1pt solid #e2e8f0;"><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><strong>Phase 8</strong></td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">Documentation</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;">User manual, project documentation, & setup guide</td><td style="padding: 6pt 10pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; color: #334155;"><code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">README.md</code> & Documentation</td></tr></table><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; margin: 16pt 0;" /><h2 style="color: #0369a1; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold; border-bottom: 1pt solid #bae6fd; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid;">19. 🎓 BEGINNER LEARNING PATH</h2><p style="font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; color: #1e293b; margin: 6pt 0;">If you are a beginner looking to learn web development by building a project like this, follow this step-by-step learning progression:</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>1.</strong> <strong>HTML5 Fundamentals:</strong> Learn document structure, semantic tags (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;"><section></code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;"><main></code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;"><header></code>), forms, and inputs.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>2.</strong> <strong>CSS3 & Glassmorphism:</strong> Master Flexbox, CSS Grid, CSS Variables, positioning, background blurs (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">backdrop-filter</code>), and media queries.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>3.</strong> <strong>JavaScript (ES6+) DOM Manipulation:</strong> Practice event handling (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">addEventListener</code>), query selectors (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">querySelectorAll</code>), array methods (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">forEach</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">filter</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">unshift</code>), and template literals.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>4.</strong> <strong>PHP Basics & Templating:</strong> Learn how PHP embeds inside HTML, handles arrays (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">foreach</code>), reads files (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">file_get_contents</code>), and formats JSON (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">json_encode</code>).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>5.</strong> <strong>Backend APIs & Asynchronous JS (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">fetch</code>):</strong> Learn how frontend JavaScript sends POST requests to PHP scripts asynchronously without reloading the page.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>6.</strong> <strong>Authentication & Security:</strong> Understand sessions (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">session_start()</code>), password hashing (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">password_hash</code>), and HTML sanitization.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>7.</strong> <strong>JSON File Databases:</strong> Practice reading, modifying, and saving structured JSON data files as a lightweight alternative to SQL databases.</p><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; margin: 16pt 0;" /><h2 style="color: #0369a1; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold; border-bottom: 1pt solid #bae6fd; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid;">20. 🏗️ BUILD A SIMILAR PROJECT FROM SCRATCH (10 MILESTONES)</h2><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">Milestone 1: Basic Application Layout</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Goal:</strong> Create simple <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">index.php</code> and <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">styles.css</code> files.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Learning Requirements:</strong> Basic HTML structure & CSS styling.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Files to Create:</strong> <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">index.php</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">styles.css</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Expected Result:</strong> A clean web page displaying a static title and bio paragraph.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Common Mistake:</strong> Forgetting to link the CSS file inside <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;"><head></code>.</p><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">Milestone 2: JSON Data Storage Setup</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Goal:</strong> Store portfolio data in a structured JSON file.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Learning Requirements:</strong> JSON syntax rules (key-value pairs, array formatting).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Files to Create:</strong> <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">data/portfolio.json</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Expected Result:</strong> Valid JSON file containing initial bio and publication arrays.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Common Mistake:</strong> Missing trailing commas or unquoted keys causing JSON syntax errors.</p><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">Milestone 3: PHP Dynamic Rendering</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Goal:</strong> Read JSON data in PHP and render it dynamically onto the page.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Learning Requirements:</strong> <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">file_get_contents()</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">json_decode()</code>, PHP <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">foreach</code> loops.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Files to Modify:</strong> <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">index.php</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Expected Result:</strong> Website automatically displays items stored in <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">portfolio.json</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Common Mistake:</strong> Not checking if <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">file_exists()</code> before calling <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">file_get_contents()</code>.</p><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">Milestone 4: Client-Side Modals & Interactivity</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Goal:</strong> Add JavaScript popups to view details when clicking a card.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Learning Requirements:</strong> JS click event listeners, modifying CSS class <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">.active</code> on modal containers.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Files to Create/Modify:</strong> <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">script.js</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">styles.css</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">index.php</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Expected Result:</strong> Clicking a button opens a modal window with full details.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Common Mistake:</strong> Forgetting to prevent default anchor behaviors or event propagation.</p><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">Milestone 5: Real-Time Live Search & Category Filters</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Goal:</strong> Build client-side text search and category buttons.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Learning Requirements:</strong> JS <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">input</code> event listeners, string <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">.includes()</code>, exact matching logic.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Files to Modify:</strong> <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">script.js</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Expected Result:</strong> Cards hide and show instantly based on search input or active filter button.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Common Mistake:</strong> Using generic substring checks that match unintended categories (e.g., "national" matching "international").</p><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">Milestone 6: Admin Login System</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Goal:</strong> Create a secure login form for the site owner.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Learning Requirements:</strong> PHP Sessions (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">session_start()</code>), <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">password_hash()</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">password_verify()</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Files to Create:</strong> <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/login.php</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/api.php</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">data/admin_creds.json</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Expected Result:</strong> Access to admin page is blocked unless valid credentials are provided.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Common Mistake:</strong> Storing passwords in plain text instead of salted BCRYPT hashes.</p><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">Milestone 7: Super Admin Management Dashboard</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Goal:</strong> Build a tabbed control panel to view, add, edit, and delete data.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Learning Requirements:</strong> Tab switching JS, building modal forms dynamically.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Files to Create:</strong> <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/index.php</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Expected Result:</strong> Fully functional desktop dashboard with tabbed section managers.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Common Mistake:</strong> Allowing table cells to wrap infinitely, causing horizontal scrollbars on desktop.</p><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">Milestone 8: Backend API REST Integration</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Goal:</strong> Connect Admin Dashboard forms to <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/api.php</code> via JS <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">fetch()</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Learning Requirements:</strong> <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">fetch()</code> POST requests, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">FormData</code>, PHP <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">json_encode()</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Files to Modify:</strong> <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/api.php</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/index.php</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Expected Result:</strong> Submitting an admin form updates <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">data/portfolio.json</code> instantly without page reloads.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Common Mistake:</strong> Not returning proper <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">Content-Type: application/json</code> headers from PHP.</p><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">Milestone 9: File Upload System</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Goal:</strong> Allow uploading PDF and image files for certificates.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Learning Requirements:</strong> HTML <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;"><input type="file"></code>, PHP <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">$_FILES</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">move_uploaded_file()</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Files to Modify:</strong> <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/api.php</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/index.php</code>.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Expected Result:</strong> Certificate files save to <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">assets/certificates/</code> and links update in the database.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Common Mistake:</strong> Not creating the destination folder before calling <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">move_uploaded_file()</code>.</p><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">Milestone 10: Final Deployment & Testing</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Goal:</strong> Test all features, lint code, and upload to hosting server.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Learning Requirements:</strong> PHP CLI syntax checking, FTP/cPanel deployment.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Files to Verify:</strong> Complete project directory.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Expected Result:</strong> Portfolio site running smoothly on a live web server.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Common Mistake:</strong> Forgetting to set directory write permissions for <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">data/</code> on Linux servers.</p><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; margin: 16pt 0;" /><h2 style="color: #0369a1; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold; border-bottom: 1pt solid #bae6fd; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid;">21. 💡 ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAMS FOR NON-TECHNICAL PEOPLE</h2><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">How the Entire Website Works (The Restaurant Analogy)</h3>
    <div style="margin: 14pt 0; padding: 12pt; background-color: #f8fafc; border: 1.5pt solid #0284c7; border-radius: 6pt; box-shadow: 0 2pt 4pt rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">
        <div style="font-family: 'Calibri', sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; color: #0369a1; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5pt; margin-bottom: 8pt; border-bottom: 1pt dashed #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 4pt;">
            📌 SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE & FLOW DIAGRAM
        </div>
        <div style="padding: 4pt 8pt; margin: 3pt 0; background-color: #ffffff; border-left: 3pt solid #0284c7; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Calibri', monospace; font-size: 9.5pt; color: #1e293b;">Customer <strong style="color: #0f172a; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 2pt 5pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 3pt;">Customer / Visitor</strong>   <span style="color: #0284c7; font-weight: bold;">➔</span>  <span style="background: #e0f2fe; color: #0369a1; padding: 2pt 6pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 8.5pt; font-weight: bold;"> <strong style="color: #0f172a; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 2pt 5pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 3pt;">1. Looks at Menu & Orders</strong> </span>  Waiter <strong style="color: #0f172a; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 2pt 5pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 3pt;">Frontend UI / Browser</strong> </div><div style="padding: 4pt 8pt; margin: 3pt 0; background-color: #ffffff; border-left: 3pt solid #0284c7; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Calibri', monospace; font-size: 9.5pt; color: #1e293b;">Waiter  <span style="color: #0284c7; font-weight: bold;">➔</span>  <span style="background: #e0f2fe; color: #0369a1; padding: 2pt 6pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 8.5pt; font-weight: bold;"> <strong style="color: #0f172a; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 2pt 5pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 3pt;">2. Takes Order to Kitchen</strong> </span>  Chef <strong style="color: #0f172a; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 2pt 5pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 3pt;">Backend API / PHP Engine</strong> </div><div style="padding: 4pt 8pt; margin: 3pt 0; background-color: #ffffff; border-left: 3pt solid #0284c7; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Calibri', monospace; font-size: 9.5pt; color: #1e293b;">Chef  <span style="color: #0284c7; font-weight: bold;">➔</span>  <span style="background: #e0f2fe; color: #0369a1; padding: 2pt 6pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 8.5pt; font-weight: bold;"> <strong style="color: #0f172a; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 2pt 5pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 3pt;">3. Retrieves Ingredients</strong> </span>  Pantry <strong style="color: #0f172a; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 2pt 5pt; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 3pt;">Filing Cabinet / JSON Database</strong> </div><div style="padding: 4pt 8pt; margin: 3pt 0; background-color: #ffffff; border-left: 3pt solid #0284c7; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Calibri', monospace; font-size: 9.5pt; color: #1e293b;">Pantry  <span style="color: #0284c7; font-weight: bold;">➔</span> >Chef: 4. Ingredients Retrieved</div><div style="padding: 4pt 8pt; margin: 3pt 0; background-color: #ffffff; border-left: 3pt solid #0284c7; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Calibri', monospace; font-size: 9.5pt; color: #1e293b;">Chef  <span style="color: #0284c7; font-weight: bold;">➔</span> >Waiter: 5. Prepares Dish</div><div style="padding: 4pt 8pt; margin: 3pt 0; background-color: #ffffff; border-left: 3pt solid #0284c7; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Calibri', monospace; font-size: 9.5pt; color: #1e293b;">Waiter  <span style="color: #0284c7; font-weight: bold;">➔</span> >Customer: 6. Serves Complete Meal / Webpage</div>
    </div>
    <h4 style="color: #0f172a; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; page-break-after: avoid;">How to Understand This Analogy</h4><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>The Customer (Visitor):</strong> You, sitting at your computer viewing the academic portfolio.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>The Waiter (Frontend):</strong> The beautiful dark screen and buttons you interact with. The waiter takes your clicks and delivers the results back to your screen.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>The Chef (Backend Engine - PHP):</strong> Working behind the kitchen doors. Receives requests from the waiter, verifies passwords, and formats data into clean pages.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>The Pantry (JSON Database):</strong> The organized shelves where all information (bio, research papers, certificates, memberships) is safely stored.</p><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; margin: 16pt 0;" /><h2 style="color: #0369a1; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold; border-bottom: 1pt solid #bae6fd; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid;">22. 📚 GLOSSARY OF TECHNICAL TERMS</h2><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>API (Application Programming Interface):</strong> A set of rules allowing the frontend user interface to talk to backend server scripts.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>BCRYPT:</strong> An advanced cryptographic hash function used to securely encrypt passwords before saving them.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>CMS (Content Management System):</strong> A web application allowing users to manage digital content without writing code.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete):</strong> The four basic operations of persistent storage.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>DOM (Document Object Model):</strong> The structural tree representation of HTML elements on a web page manipulated by JavaScript.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Fetch API:</strong> Modern JavaScript method for sending network requests to the server asynchronously in the background.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Glassmorphism:</strong> A visual design trend featuring dark translucent card backgrounds, subtle light borders, and background blur effects.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>JSON (JavaScript Object Notation):</strong> A lightweight, human-readable data format used to store and exchange information.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>REST (Representational State Transfer):</strong> An architectural style for web APIs using standard HTTP requests.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>Session:</strong> A way to store information (like logged-in status) across multiple web page requests.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>SPA (Single Page Application):</strong> A web application that fits on a single web page for fluid user interaction.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;">• <strong>XAMPP:</strong> A free, cross-platform local web server package containing Apache, MariaDB, and PHP.</p><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; margin: 16pt 0;" /><h2 style="color: #0369a1; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold; border-bottom: 1pt solid #bae6fd; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid;">23. ✅ DEVELOPER CHECKLIST</h2><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">Before Development</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Understand the problem statement and domain requirements.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Identify user roles (Visitors vs Super Admin).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Define portfolio data schemas (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">about</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">research</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">certs</code>, <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">memberships</code>).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Select tech stack (PHP, JavaScript, CSS3, JSON).</p><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">During Development</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Initialize local XAMPP web server environment.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Build dark glassmorphic responsive frontend template (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">index.php</code>).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Program client-side search, filters, and modal document inspection (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">script.js</code>).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Construct JSON file database (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">data/portfolio.json</code>).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Build backend API controller (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/api.php</code>).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Develop secure session and BCRYPT login wall (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/login.php</code>).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Create 10-tab Super Admin Panel (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/index.php</code>).</p><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">Before Release</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Run PHP syntax verification (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">php -l</code>) across all scripts.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Test exact category filtering (National vs International) to prevent collisions.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Ensure zero horizontal scrollbars on desktop viewports (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">table-layout: fixed</code>).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Verify top-insertion (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">unshift</code>) for new admin entries.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Update documentation and setup instructions (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">README.md</code>).</p><h3 style="color: #0284c7; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid;">After Release</h3><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Monitor server performance and error logs.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Verify file write permissions on production host.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><span style="color: #16a34a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;">[✔]</span> Backup <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">data/portfolio.json</code> regularly.</p><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; margin: 16pt 0;" /><h2 style="color: #0369a1; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold; border-bottom: 1pt solid #bae6fd; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid;">24. 📜 DOCUMENTATION RULES ADHERED TO</h2><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>1.</strong> <strong>Grounded in Source Code:</strong> Every file path, database entity, API action, and feature described in this guide is derived directly from the actual codebase.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>2.</strong> <strong>Zero Information Invention:</strong> No fictitious technologies, frameworks, or routes were added.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>3.</strong> <strong>Beginner Clarity:</strong> Complex technical concepts are explained alongside real-world analogies.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>4.</strong> <strong>Comprehensive Structure:</strong> Follows a logical 25-section architecture covering every stage of software engineering from zero to production deployment.</p><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; margin: 16pt 0;" /><h2 style="color: #0369a1; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold; border-bottom: 1pt solid #bae6fd; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid;">25. ❓ FINAL QUALITY CHECK (17 BEGINNER QUESTIONS ANSWERED)</h2><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>1.</strong> <strong>What problem does this project solve?</strong> It provides academic faculty with a unified portfolio website and a web-based CMS to manage research publications, verified IDs (ORCID, Scopus, Vidwan ID <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">521179</code>), certificates, and memberships without editing code.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>2.</strong> <strong>Who uses it?</strong> Academic evaluators, students, researchers (viewers), and the faculty member (Super Admin).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>3.</strong> <strong>What technologies are used?</strong> PHP, JavaScript (ES6+), HTML5, CSS3, JSON, Apache.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>4.</strong> <strong>What does each technology do?</strong> HTML structures pages; CSS styles the glassmorphic UI; JavaScript handles modals and filtering; PHP runs backend operations; JSON acts as the database.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>5.</strong> <strong>How does frontend work?</strong> Displays cards and sections, captures user clicks/searches, and opens popups.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>6.</strong> <strong>How does backend work?</strong> Receives requests from the frontend, checks login authorization, and updates JSON files or stores uploaded documents.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>7.</strong> <strong>How does the database work?</strong> Reads and writes data to structured JSON files (<code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">portfolio.json</code>) without needing an SQL server.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>8.</strong> <strong>How does frontend communicate with backend?</strong> Via asynchronous HTTP requests using the JavaScript <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">fetch()</code> API.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>9.</strong> <strong>How does authentication work?</strong> Passes credentials to <code style="font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; background-color: #f1f5f9; color: #0284c7; padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; font-size: 10pt;">admin/api.php</code>, verifies them against stored BCRYPT hashes, and starts a secure PHP session.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>10.</strong> <strong>How does each major feature work?</strong> Detailed step-by-step breakdowns are provided in Section 12.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>11.</strong> <strong>How does data move through the system?</strong> User Action -> JS Event -> Fetch Request -> PHP Controller -> JSON Database File -> Response -> UI Update.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>12.</strong> <strong>How is it tested?</strong> Through PHP CLI syntax checking, manual UI workflow testing, and network payload inspection.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>13.</strong> <strong>How is it deployed?</strong> By copying files to an Apache server (XAMPP locally or cPanel/Linux VPS in production) and configuring permissions.</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>14.</strong> <strong>What should I learn to build something similar?</strong> HTML -> CSS -> JavaScript -> PHP -> REST APIs -> Data Persistence (Section 19).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>15.</strong> <strong>What should I build first?</strong> A basic static page (Milestone 1).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>16.</strong> <strong>What should I build next?</strong> Move data into a JSON file and load it with PHP (Milestone 2 & 3).</p><p style="margin: 3pt 0 3pt 18pt; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #334155;"><strong>17.</strong> <strong>How do all components connect?</strong> Rendered in the Complete System Architecture Diagram in Section 17.</p><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; margin: 16pt 0;" /><p style="font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; color: #1e293b; margin: 6pt 0;"><em>Documentation generated and validated for the Academic Portfolio & Super Admin Content Management System.</em></p>

